⟦2800⟧At the limit of dilution, when the concentration of a solution approaches zero, we have seen that thermodynamical theory,
{{EB1911 Shoulder Heading|Osmotic Pressure.}}
verified by experiment, shows that the osmotic pressure has the same value as the gas pressure of the same number of molecules in the same space. Gases at high pressures fail to conform to Boyle's law, and solu-

